  "M-lik": "physics in likelihood; model-error knob = sigma_r (fixed residual pseudo-noise). eps=0 control: final |theta_mean - 1.15| = 0.001, final SD = 0.001 (concentrates on theta_true). DISCRETIZATION-INVARIANCE: ~invariant to the genuine mesh knob N_c (spread 0.005/0.002 for eps 0/0.3) BUT DRIFTS with the FICTITIOUS residual noise sigma_r (spread 0.084/0.084) with no principled way to set it. => the discretization-dependence charge is PARTIALLY supported and sharpened: the sensitivity is to sigma_r, not the mesh. under eps=0.3 (model-form error) theta is biased to 1.269 (truth 1.15); so the parameter is NOT recovered under model error -- a shared limit.",
  "M-statfem": "physics in likelihood (data = FE + discrepancy); model-error knob = sigma_d (learned additive discrepancy). eps=0 control: final |theta_mean - 1.15| = 0.000, final SD = 0.001 (concentrates on theta_true). DISCRETIZATION-INVARIANCE: ~invariant to mesh h (spread 0.003/0.002); the learned discrepancy sigma_d stays small under eps=0.3, so theta ABSORBS the omitted foundation (discrepancy/parameter confounding) rather than the discrepancy flagging it. under eps=0.3 (model-form error) theta is biased to 1.272 (truth 1.15); so the parameter is NOT recovered under model error -- a shared limit.",
  "M-ift": "physics in prior; model-error knob = beta (learned inverse-temperature). eps=0 control: final |theta_mean - 1.15| = 0.000, final SD = 0.001 (concentrates on theta_true). DISCRETIZATION-INVARIANCE: ~invariant to N_c (spread 0.003/0.004); the physics weight beta is LEARNED, so there is no fictitious sigma_r knob; in this toy beta is weakly identified above a threshold but theta is unaffected. under eps=0.3 (model-form error) theta is biased to 1.267 (truth 1.15); so the parameter is NOT recovered under model error -- a shared limit."
